<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  keeper's iOS privacy manifest (Epic 62, Story 62.6). Lives under keeper_iOS/, which
  project.yml lists as a source folder, so XcodeGen adds it to the app target's resources
  and it ships in the bundle root as Apple requires.

  What voice adds, and why each entry is what it is:

  - NSPrivacyTracking is false and NSPrivacyTrackingDomains is empty: keeper has no
    tracking and no analytics, on any platform (docs/egress.md is the complete list of
    destinations, and none is a tracker).
  - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty even though the app hears audio: Apple defines
    "collected" as data transmitted off the device. Speech is recognised on the device
    (`requiresOnDeviceRecognition = true`, no server fallback, NFR-50) and what is sent to
    the model endpoint the person configured is the TEXT they chose to send, to a server
    they chose — not data keeper collects. The audio itself is never stored or sent.
  - NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes: the microphone and the Speech framework are governed by
    their usage-description strings and the permission dialogs (FR-408), and are NOT in
    Apple's "required reason" API list, so voice adds no entry here. The list is empty
    because this manifest records what voice requires; an audit of the whole binary for
    file-timestamp / UserDefaults / disk-space reasons is a release task (Story 62.7).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
